    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by an elite offensive profile from **Corbin Carroll**, who leads our squad with an 87.14 efficiency score against Mikolas. The combination of an advantageous matchup against a high-xERA starter and **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s stolen base upside\u2014bolstered by a favorable, slow-delivery opponent\u2014makes him our clear priority. Similarly, **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** benefit from strong platoon positioning against favorable right-handed arms, while **James Wood** remains a must-start despite facing a lefty; his elite 0.423 xwOBA ensures he maintains a high floor even without a platoon advantage. **Austin Riley** is also positioned for a productive outing, as his score climbed to 71.27 largely due to a significant park factor boost and the benefit of a slow-delivery opposing pitcher that invites aggressive baserunning.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Seiya Suzuki**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 47.00 score. While his presence in the top of the order provides value, the efficiency gains from our mid-lineup bats in more favorable matchups pushed him out of the primary slots. We are exercising caution with **Josh Naylor** and **Mickey Moniak** today; both face high-skill pitchers (deGrom and Misiorowski, respectively) with xERAs near or below 3.00, suppressing their overall outlook. We have opted to bench **Cole Young** and **Travis Bazzana** entirely, as both fell below our 40.0 efficiency floor due to the combination of tough opposing pitching and lack of elite baserunning upside for this specific slate. Keep a close watch on the weather and any late lineup shifts, particularly for those players facing pitchers with sub-4.00 xERAs, as the volatility of the arm talent on display today introduces higher-than-average risk.",
